            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اعصاب (a'sâb) — \"nerves\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "صدای بلند روی اعصاب من است. sedâ-ye boland ru-ye a'sâb-e man ast. Loud noise gets on my nerves."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A plural noun. ru-ye a'sâb budan — to get on someone's nerves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "a'sâb is a loan, usually traced to Arabic aʿṣāb, the plural of ʿaṣab, 'nerve, sinew'. The same 'asab is inside 'asabâni. EtymDB has no entry for it."
            }
          ]
        },
